<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Africa Squadron</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1808">1808</a>–<a href="/years/1867">1867</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Preventative Squadron</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a> Squadron was the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a> force created in 1808 to suppress the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a> after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> abolished it in 1807. Patrolling the West African coast from bases such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/freetown">Freetown</a>, it captured about 1,600 slave ships and freed some 150,000 Africans before being merged into a wider command in 1867.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-africa-squadron.jpg" alt="West Africa Squadron" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Irwin John David Bevan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HMS_Black_Joke_(1827)_and_prizes.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
